0010:     """
0011:     Recolor the sparse foreground pixels in scan order along their longer spread, cycling red, teal, and grey.
0012: 
0013:     Input structure:
0014:     - The dominant color is the background.
0015:     - Every foreground object is a single isolated 4-connected pixel.
0016:     - The foreground pixel set has a rectangular bbox whose row or column extent defines the scan direction.
0017: 
0018:     Rule:
0019:     - Keep the background unchanged.
0020:     - If the foreground bbox is at least as tall as it is wide, order foreground pixels row-major; otherwise order them column-major.
0021:     - Recolor the ordered pixels by repeating red, teal, grey from the first pixel onward.
0022: 
0023:     Key insight:
0024:     - The original foreground colors are only markers; the output color depends on each marker's ordinal position in the dominant scan direction.
0025:     """
